/* Airline Agent Policy — tau2 airline domain (variant-set run 2)

   Source spec:  experiments/translation/spec.md
   Trace evidence: outputs/variant-set/run2/scenarios.json
                   (74 captured, oracle-labeled decision points)
   System profile: outputs/variant-set/run2/system.md

   Enforcement target: LLMAgent, the airline customer-service agent.
   Every decision point in the capture is a CallTool action; the
   agent's plain messages to the customer are not checked by this
   deployment, so clauses about what the agent may *say* are recorded
   below as not encoded rather than faked.

   Content checks use the deterministic C++ matchers in
   airline_functors.cpp (no @llm_check_fn, no @ask, no
   ActionMetadata — none of the three is supported by this
   deployment, and a rule built on one would silently never fire).
*/
// Round-trip audit: PASS (2026-08-20). Reading the rules alone and
// restating them in English against the spec found three defects,
// all fixed and covered by new probes: a reservation was read as
// basic economy if ANY snapshot said so (an upgrade made earlier in
// the same conversation was ignored); a flight change could be paid
// from an unverified profile while a booking could not; and a
// get_flight_status answer was matched conversation-wide instead of
// against the reservation whose flight it describes, so an unrelated
// cancelled flight could authorize a cancellation and set a
// compensation rate.
#include "../../../../policies/common_policy.dl"

/* ── K-Constraints (verified against the captured traces) ─────────

   K1: Two agent names speak in this system and BOTH emit
       $UserRole() turns (system.md "Role collisions"):
         - LLMAgent   / $UserRole()  = the customer's own words
         - UserSimulator / $UserRole() = the airline agent's words,
           mirrored into the simulator's view (node e9c9a779
           "Hi! How can I help you today?" is the same text as
           LLMAgent/assistant node 7d161045).
       Every rule that reads customer content therefore filters on
       BOTH msg.agent = "LLMAgent" AND msg.agent_role = $UserRole().
       Without the agent filter the airline agent could confirm its
       own booking changes.

   K2: Tool results are graph nodes with msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
       msg.agent_role = $AgentType(), marked by ToolResult(id, fn, _);
       the payload is the node's msg.contents. The 74 captured slices
       carry 238 such nodes, so ToolResult joins do fire here.

   K3: get_user_details results are JSON objects carrying membership
       as a bare string ("regular" | "silver" | "gold") and
       payment_methods as an OBJECT keyed by payment id — not a list.
       (e.g. user omar_rossi_1241: membership "gold",
       payment_methods keys gift_card_8190333, credit_card_6754990,
       certificate_8390038, ...)

   K4: get_reservation_details, cancel_reservation and every
       update_reservation_* call return the same reservation object:
       reservation_id, user_id, cabin, created_at ("2024-05-01T04:50:18"),
       insurance ("yes" | "no"), passengers[], total_baggages,
       nonfree_baggages, flights[] with flight_number and date.
       All five tools are therefore read for reservation state.

   K5: get_flight_status, search_direct_flight, search_onestop_flight
       and calculate return bare strings, NOT JSON objects (system.md
       warnings). Flight status is the whole payload ("delayed",
       "landed", "available"), so it is matched as a substring and
       never with a field accessor.

   K6: send_certificate and transfer_to_human_agents produce no
       result node at all (system.md warnings), so no rule may join
       on their ToolResult.

   K7: Exactly one incoming edge of the current node carries
       proximal = 1 in EdgeData: the turn immediately before the tool
       call. Confirmation is keyed on that edge, because "obtain
       explicit user confirmation to proceed" means the go-ahead is
       what triggers the write, not that a "yes" appears somewhere in
       the history.

   K8: One assistant turn can propose several tool calls, and the
       reference monitor checks each of them separately against an
       identical graph (node a950ffbd proposes 3 writes; the oracle
       allowed 2 of the 3). A rule keyed on the size of the batch
       therefore cannot distinguish members of that batch — see the
       not-encoded list below.

   K9: One reservation id can appear several times in a slice with
       different cabin / baggage values (before and after an update).
       Rules that must hold for every observed state (passenger
       count, bag monotonicity) quantify over all snapshots; rules
       that need only one witness (eligibility) quantify existentially.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Structured Spec ──────────────────────────────────────────────
   C1:  Allow the read-only tools (get_user_details,
        get_reservation_details, search_direct_flight,
        search_onestop_flight, get_flight_status, calculate,
        list_all_airports) — retrieval changes no booking.
   C2:  Allow transfer_to_human_agents (the spec's escape hatch for
        requests outside the agent's scope).
   C3:  Allow the booking-database writes and send_certificate as a
        baseline, then carve them with the denials below.
   C4:  Deny any tool outside the airline agent's toolset (no
        IsAuthorized rule matches it).
   C5:  Deny a booking-database write (book_reservation,
        cancel_reservation, update_reservation_flights,
        update_reservation_baggages, update_reservation_passengers)
        unless the immediately preceding turn is the customer's
        explicit confirmation.
   C6:  Deny a write to a reservation whose details were never
        retrieved in this conversation — the agent must obtain the
        reservation id and check the rules before calling the API.
   C7:  Deny update_reservation_passengers that changes the NUMBER of
        passengers.
   C8:  Deny update_reservation_baggages that lowers the bag count
        (bags may be added, never removed).
   C9:  Deny update_reservation_flights that changes the flights of a
        basic-economy reservation (basic economy cannot be modified;
        a cabin-only change keeps the same flights and is allowed).
        A reservation counts as basic economy only when every
        snapshot of it in this conversation says so, so an upgrade
        made earlier in the same conversation takes effect.
   C10: Deny update_reservation_flights on a reservation with an
        already-flown segment.
   C11: Deny update_reservation_flights paid with a travel
        certificate, with a payment id absent from the user's profile,
        or when the profile was never retrieved and so the payment id
        cannot be checked (a single gift card or credit card already
        in the profile is required).
   C12: Deny book_reservation with more than five passengers.
   C13: Deny book_reservation using more than one travel certificate,
        more than one credit card, or more than three gift cards.
   C14: Deny book_reservation with a payment method that is not
        already in the user's profile.
   C15: Deny book_reservation when the booking user's profile was
        never retrieved (the agent must obtain the user id first).
   C16: Deny cancel_reservation when any portion of the flight has
        already been flown (a human agent is needed).
   C17: Deny cancel_reservation unless one of the four grounds holds:
        booked within the last 24 hours, the airline cancelled a
        flight OF THIS RESERVATION, the cabin is business, or the
        reservation has travel insurance and the customer stated a
        covered reason.
   C18: Deny cancel_reservation when the customer never stated a
        reason for cancelling.
   C19: Deny send_certificate to a regular member — regular members
        are never eligible for compensation.
   C20: Deny send_certificate when the membership level was never
        verified against the user's profile.
   C21: Deny send_certificate when the customer never asked for
        compensation (it must not be offered proactively).
   C22: Deny send_certificate whose amount is not $50 per passenger
        for a confirmed delay or $100 per passenger for a confirmed
        airline cancellation, counted on the passengers of the very
        reservation whose flight carries that status.
   C23: Return an error for any denied tool call rather than letting
        it pass through.
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   Clauses deliberately NOT encoded, with the reason:

   N1: "You should only make one tool call at a time." Each call in a
       batch is checked separately against an identical graph (K8),
       so no per-action rule can allow the first and deny the rest;
       and the trace labels allow batched read calls and 2 of 3
       batched writes. Encoding it would deny calls the evidence
       allows.
   N2: The free checked-bag allowance (0-4 bags by membership and
       cabin, $50 per extra bag). The captured runs contain writes
       with a demonstrably wrong nonfree_baggages that the oracle
       allowed on the ground that the customer confirmed the price,
       so an arithmetic gate here would contradict the trace
       evidence. The confirmation rule (C5) is what protects the
       customer from an unwanted charge.
   N3: "The user cannot add insurance after initial booking." No
       update_reservation_* tool takes an insurance argument
       (system.md argument fields), so the action is unreachable
       through the API this policy guards.
   N4: "Cabin class must be the same across all flights." Both
       book_reservation and update_reservation_flights take a single
       cabin argument for the whole reservation, so the API shape
       already enforces it.
   N5: Rules about what the agent may SAY (no outside knowledge, no
       subjective recommendations, the transfer wording, listing
       action details before asking). This deployment authorizes tool
       calls only; no SendAttempt action reaches the policy.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Custom content functors (airline_functors.cpp) ─────────────── */

.functor user_affirms(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor states_cancel_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor covered_cancel_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor requests_compensation(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor flight_list_sig(json: symbol): symbol stateful
.functor any_flight_before(json: symbol, iso_date: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor flight_list_has(json: symbol, flight_number: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor res_passenger_count(json: symbol): number stateful
.functor count_payment_kind(args: symbol, prefix: symbol): number stateful
.functor payments_in_profile(args: symbol, profile: symbol): unsigned stateful

/* ── Tool classes ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */

// C1: retrieval only — no booking state changes.
.decl ReadOnlyTool(name: symbol)
ReadOnlyTool("get_user_details").
ReadOnlyTool("get_reservation_details").
ReadOnlyTool("search_direct_flight").
ReadOnlyTool("search_onestop_flight").
ReadOnlyTool("get_flight_status").
ReadOnlyTool("calculate").
ReadOnlyTool("list_all_airports").

// C5: writes to the booking database, which need confirmation.
.decl BookingWriteTool(name: symbol)
BookingWriteTool("book_reservation").
BookingWriteTool("cancel_reservation").
BookingWriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
BookingWriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
BookingWriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").

// C6: writes that name an existing reservation.
.decl ReservationWriteTool(name: symbol)
ReservationWriteTool("cancel_reservation").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").
ReservationWriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").

// K4: tools whose result payload is a reservation object.
.decl ReturnsReservation(name: symbol)
ReturnsReservation("get_reservation_details").
ReturnsReservation("book_reservation").
ReturnsReservation("cancel_reservation").
ReturnsReservation("update_reservation_flights").
ReturnsReservation("update_reservation_baggages").
ReturnsReservation("update_reservation_passengers").

/* ── Graph traversal gate ──────────────────────────────────────── */

// Only the write tools and send_certificate consult prior context;
// the read tools are authorized on their name alone, so they skip
// the backward slice entirely. ReachableFrom is never referenced by
// this policy, so its gate stays empty and the pairwise closure is
// never built.
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :-
    Actions(_, a), IsTool(a, t), BookingWriteTool(t).
CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :-
    Actions(_, a), IsTool(a, "send_certificate").

/* ── Conversation helpers ──────────────────────────────────────── */

// K1: the customer's own turns — agent name AND role, never role alone.
.decl CustomerTurn(id: symbol, text: symbol)
CustomerTurn(id, text) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole(),
    text = msg.contents,
    text != "".

// K7: the turn immediately before the tool call under evaluation.
.decl ProximalCustomerTurn(text: symbol)
ProximalCustomerTurn(text) :-
    Current(dst),
    EdgeData(src, dst, [prox, _]),
    prox = 1,
    CustomerTurn(src, text).

// C5: the customer's explicit go-ahead triggered this write.
.decl CustomerConfirmed()
CustomerConfirmed() :-
    ProximalCustomerTurn(text),
    @user_affirms(text) = 1.

// C18 / C17: reasons the customer stated anywhere in this conversation.
.decl CancelReasonStated()
CancelReasonStated() :-
    CustomerTurn(_, text),
    @states_cancel_reason(text) = 1.

.decl CoveredReasonStated()
CoveredReasonStated() :-
    CustomerTurn(_, text),
    @covered_cancel_reason(text) = 1.

// C21: compensation must be asked for, never offered proactively.
.decl CompensationRequested()
CompensationRequested() :-
    CustomerTurn(_, text),
    @requests_compensation(text) = 1.

/* ── Tool-result helpers ───────────────────────────────────────── */

// K2: a tool result inside the current backward slice.
.decl SliceResult(id: symbol, tool: symbol, body: symbol)
SliceResult(id, tool, body) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, tool, _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    body = msg.contents,
    body != "".

// K4 / K9: every reservation snapshot observed in this conversation.
.decl ReservationState(res_id: symbol, body: symbol)
ReservationState(rid, body) :-
    SliceResult(_, tool, body),
    ReturnsReservation(tool),
    rid = @json_get_str(body, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

.decl ReservationSeen(res_id: symbol)
ReservationSeen(rid) :- ReservationState(rid, _).

// K3: the customer's profile as returned by get_user_details.
.decl UserProfile(user_id: symbol, body: symbol)
UserProfile(uid, body) :-
    SliceResult(_, "get_user_details", body),
    uid = @json_get_str(body, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl ProfileSeen(user_id: symbol)
ProfileSeen(uid) :- UserProfile(uid, _).

.decl MemberLevel(user_id: symbol, level: symbol)
MemberLevel(uid, level) :-
    UserProfile(uid, body),
    level = @json_get_str(body, "membership"),
    level != "".

.decl CompensationEligibleMember(user_id: symbol)
CompensationEligibleMember(uid) :- MemberLevel(uid, "silver").
CompensationEligibleMember(uid) :- MemberLevel(uid, "gold").

// K5: a flight status is the whole (non-JSON) payload, and the flight
// it describes is named in the ToolResult arguments, not in the body.
// Joining the two ties the answer to the reservation that carries that
// flight, so a cancelled flight the customer never booked cannot
// authorize anything.
.decl FlightStatusFor(res_id: symbol, status: symbol)
FlightStatusFor(rid, status) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_flight_status", targs),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    status = @str_to_lower(msg.contents),
    status != "",
    number = @json_get_str(targs, "flight_number"),
    number != "",
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    @flight_list_has(body, number) = 1.

.decl AirlineCancelledFlight(res_id: symbol)
AirlineCancelledFlight(rid) :-
    FlightStatusFor(rid, status),
    @str_contains(status, "cancel") = 1.

.decl DelayConfirmed(res_id: symbol)
DelayConfirmed(rid) :-
    FlightStatusFor(rid, status),
    @str_contains(status, "delayed") = 1.

// C10 / C16: "2024-05-15 15:00:00 EST" is the spec's current time, so
// a segment dated before 2024-05-15 has already been flown.
.decl HasFlownSegment(res_id: symbol)
HasFlownSegment(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    @any_flight_before(body, "2024-05-15") = 1.

/* ── C1-C3: baseline authorization ─────────────────────────────── */

/* C1: read-only tools are authorized on their name alone. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    ReadOnlyTool(name).

/* C2: transfer to a human agent is always available. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "transfer_to_human_agents").

/* C3: booking writes are authorized, then carved by C5-C18. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    BookingWriteTool(name).

/* C3: compensation is authorized, then carved by C19-C22. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate").

/* C4: any other tool falls through with no IsAuthorized rule and is
   denied by the engine's allowlist semantics. */

/* ── C5: explicit confirmation before a booking write ──────────── */

// @deny_message: This change to the booking database was not confirmed by the customer. The turn immediately before this call is not an explicit go-ahead.
// @suggestion: List the exact action details (flights, cabin, passengers, baggage, payment and total price) in a message to the customer, ask them to reply "yes" to proceed, and make this call only after that reply.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    BookingWriteTool(name),
    !CustomerConfirmed().

/* ── C6: the reservation must have been retrieved first ────────── */

// @deny_message: The details of this reservation were never retrieved in this conversation, so the policy rules for the change cannot have been checked. The API does not check them for you.
// @suggestion: Call get_reservation_details for this reservation id first (use get_user_details to locate it if the customer does not know it), verify the change is allowed, then retry.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    ReservationWriteTool(name),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    !ReservationSeen(rid).

/* ── C7: the number of passengers may never change ─────────────── */

// @deny_message: This call changes the number of passengers on the reservation. The number of passengers cannot be modified — not by the agent and not by a human agent.
// @suggestion: Submit exactly as many passengers as the reservation already has, changing only their names and dates of birth. To travel with a different number of people the customer must cancel and rebook.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    proposed = @res_passenger_count(args),
    current = @res_passenger_count(body),
    proposed != current.

/* ── C8: checked bags may be added, never removed ──────────────── */

// @deny_message: This call lowers the number of checked bags on the reservation. Checked bags can be added but not removed.
// @suggestion: Set total_baggages to at least the number already on the reservation.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    proposed = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    current = @json_get_int(body, "total_baggages"),
    proposed < current.

/* ── C9: basic-economy flights cannot be changed ───────────────── */

// A cabin-only change keeps the same flight numbers and dates, which
// the spec allows for every cabin including basic economy.
.decl FlightsUnchanged(idx: unsigned)
FlightsUnchanged(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    proposed = @flight_list_sig(args),
    current = @flight_list_sig(body),
    proposed = current,
    proposed != "".

// @deny_message: This reservation is basic economy, and basic economy flights cannot be modified. Only the cabin class may be changed, keeping the same flights.
// @suggestion: Keep every flight number and date exactly as booked and change only the cabin, or explain to the customer that a basic economy itinerary cannot be rebooked.
// A reservation counts as basic economy only if EVERY snapshot of it
// in this conversation says so. Without an ordering over snapshots
// that is the safe reading: a reservation upgraded out of basic
// economy earlier in the same conversation is no longer basic
// economy, and its flights may then be changed.
.decl NonBasicSnapshot(res_id: symbol)
NonBasicSnapshot(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    cabin = @json_get_str(body, "cabin"),
    cabin != "basic_economy",
    cabin != "".

.decl BasicEconomyReservation(res_id: symbol)
BasicEconomyReservation(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    cabin = @json_get_str(body, "cabin"),
    cabin = "basic_economy",
    !NonBasicSnapshot(rid).

Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    BasicEconomyReservation(rid),
    !FlightsUnchanged(idx).

/* ── C10: nothing may be changed after a segment has flown ─────── */

// @deny_message: A flight in this reservation has already been flown, so its flights and cabin can no longer be changed.
// @suggestion: Tell the customer that a reservation with a flown segment cannot be modified, and transfer to a human agent if they need more.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    HasFlownSegment(rid).

/* ── C11: flight changes are paid by one gift card or credit card ─ */

// @deny_message: A travel certificate cannot pay for a flight change. A single gift card or credit card is required.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer which gift card or credit card from their profile to use, and pass that payment_id.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    @str_starts_with(pid, "certificate") = 1.

// @deny_message: The payment method for this change is not in the customer's profile. For safety, only payment methods already saved in the profile may be used.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details, read back the saved gift cards and credit cards, and ask the customer to pick one of those.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    uid = @json_get_str(body, "user_id"),
    UserProfile(uid, profile),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    pid != "",
    @json_object_has_key(profile, "payment_methods", pid) = 0.

// @deny_message: The customer's profile has not been retrieved, so the payment method for this change cannot be checked against it.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer for their user id, call get_user_details, and pay with one of the gift cards or credit cards saved there.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    uid = @json_get_str(body, "user_id"),
    uid != "",
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    pid != "",
    !ProfileSeen(uid).

/* ── C12: at most five passengers per reservation ──────────────── */

// @deny_message: A reservation can have at most five passengers.
// @suggestion: Split the party across separate reservations of at most five passengers each.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @res_passenger_count(args),
    n > 5.

/* ── C13: payment mix limits ───────────────────────────────────── */

// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most one travel certificate.
// @suggestion: Use a single travel certificate and cover the rest with one credit card or up to three gift cards, then re-confirm the new breakdown with the customer.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_kind(args, "certificate"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most one credit card.
// @suggestion: Charge a single credit card, adding gift cards or one travel certificate if more funds are needed.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_kind(args, "credit_card"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation can use at most three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Use no more than three gift cards and cover any remainder with one credit card or one travel certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_kind(args, "gift_card"),
    n > 3.

/* ── C14/C15: payment methods must be in the customer's profile ── */

// @deny_message: The customer's profile has not been retrieved, so this booking's payment methods cannot be verified against it.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer for their user id, call get_user_details, and book only with the payment methods saved there.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    !ProfileSeen(uid).

// @deny_message: This booking uses a payment method that is not saved in the customer's profile. For safety, only saved payment methods may be used.
// @suggestion: Read the saved payment methods back to the customer and rebuild the payment breakdown from those ids only.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    UserProfile(uid, profile),
    @payments_in_profile(args, profile) = 0.

/* ── C16: a flown reservation cannot be cancelled here ─────────── */

// @deny_message: Part of this reservation has already been flown, so it cannot be cancelled by the agent.
// @suggestion: Tell the customer this needs a human agent, call transfer_to_human_agents, and then send the transfer message.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    HasFlownSegment(rid).

/* ── C17: cancellation needs one of the four grounds ───────────── */

// Booked within the last 24 hours of the spec's current time.
.decl CancelGroundRecent(res_id: symbol)
CancelGroundRecent(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    created = @json_get_str(body, "created_at"),
    created != "",
    hours = @hours_between(created, "2024-05-15T15:00:00"),
    hours >= 0,
    hours <= 24.

.decl CancelGroundBusiness(res_id: symbol)
CancelGroundBusiness(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    cabin = @json_get_str(body, "cabin"),
    cabin = "business".

.decl CancelGroundAirline(res_id: symbol)
CancelGroundAirline(rid) :-
    AirlineCancelledFlight(rid).

.decl CancelGroundInsurance(res_id: symbol)
CancelGroundInsurance(rid) :-
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    insurance = @json_get_str(body, "insurance"),
    insurance = "yes",
    CoveredReasonStated().

.decl CancelAllowed(res_id: symbol)
CancelAllowed(rid) :- CancelGroundRecent(rid).
CancelAllowed(rid) :- CancelGroundBusiness(rid).
CancelAllowed(rid) :- CancelGroundAirline(rid).
CancelAllowed(rid) :- CancelGroundInsurance(rid).

// @deny_message: This reservation does not meet any cancellation ground: it was not booked in the last 24 hours, no flight on it was cancelled by the airline, it is not a business cabin, and it has no travel insurance covering the customer's reason.
// @suggestion: Explain which ground is missing. If the customer has travel insurance, ask whether the reason is health, weather or another significant personal circumstance; otherwise offer to transfer to a human agent.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    ReservationSeen(rid),
    !CancelAllowed(rid).

/* ── C18: the customer must state a reason ─────────────────────── */

// @deny_message: The customer has not given a reason for cancelling. The reason is required before a cancellation.
// @suggestion: Ask whether this is a change of plan, a flight the airline cancelled, or another reason, and repeat the cancellation once they answer.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    !CancelReasonStated().

/* ── C19/C20: compensation is for silver and gold members only ─── */

// @deny_message: This customer is a regular member. Regular members are not eligible for any compensation, whatever the cabin, insurance or reason — including when they say they hold a higher tier.
// @suggestion: Tell the customer their membership level on file is regular and that compensation is limited to silver and gold members. Offer to transfer to a human agent if they dispute the level.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    MemberLevel(uid, "regular").

// @deny_message: This customer's membership level has not been verified. Membership must always be checked before compensation is offered.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details for this user id and read the membership field before sending a certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    !CompensationEligibleMember(uid),
    !MemberLevel(uid, "regular").

/* ── C21: compensation only on request ─────────────────────────── */

// @deny_message: The customer has not asked for compensation. Compensation must not be offered proactively.
// @suggestion: Handle the customer's actual request. Send a certificate only if they ask for compensation themselves.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !CompensationRequested().

/* ── C22: the amount follows the schedule ──────────────────────── */

// $50 per passenger for a confirmed delay.
.decl CompensationAmountOk(idx: unsigned)
CompensationAmountOk(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    amount = @json_get_int(args, "amount"),
    DelayConfirmed(rid),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    passengers = @res_passenger_count(body),
    passengers > 0,
    amount = 50 * passengers.

// $100 per passenger for a flight the airline cancelled.
CompensationAmountOk(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    amount = @json_get_int(args, "amount"),
    AirlineCancelledFlight(rid),
    ReservationState(rid, body),
    passengers = @res_passenger_count(body),
    passengers > 0,
    amount = 100 * passengers.

// @deny_message: This certificate amount does not match the compensation schedule. A confirmed delay is worth $50 per passenger and a flight cancelled by the airline $100 per passenger, counted on a reservation whose details were retrieved in this conversation.
// @suggestion: Confirm the flight status with get_flight_status and the passenger count with get_reservation_details, then send exactly $50 or $100 times that passenger count.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !CompensationAmountOk(idx).

/* ── C23: denied tool calls return an error ────────────────────── */

DenyUnauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsToolCall(a).
